{"id": "EUVD-2026-103465", "enisaUuid": "f4be4583-94ad-3d81-9e3d-2fe959605263", "description": "libtta through 2.3 contains a stack out-of-bounds read and write vulnerability in tta_decoder_process_stream() and tta_decoder_process_frame() because header checks never reject a zero channel count. Attackers can supply a crafted .tta file declaring zero channels so decorrelation accesses cache[-1] with stream-derived values, corrupting stack memory in decoding applications.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T11:38:34", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T16:38:35", "baseScore": 4.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:L/VI:L/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haindpwn/libtta-seek-table-count-overflow-oob-write", "https://github.com/gchudov/libtta/blob/af8dc48ce859e98842ab1a3eec98416d22a5199e/libtta.c#L618", "https://github.com/gchudov/libtta/blob/af8dc48ce859e98842ab1a3eec98416d22a5199e/libtta.c#L715-L730", "https://sourceforge.net/projects/tta/", "https://github.com/gchudov/libtta", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/libtta-through-2.3-stack-out-of-bounds-write-via-zero-channel-count"], "aliases": ["GHSA-5v95-f854-g2v7", "CVE-2026-112012"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "2d5c7cb1-8263-3f4d-8008-b9794bb2ac71", "product": {"name": "libtta", "vendor": {"name": "True Audio"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22642.3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "cc85fa77-1a6d-3479-9bc1-a0bc7d743844", "vendor": {"name": "True Audio"}}], "isExploited": false}